"critique":"The four menu cards are not a coherent component system. Card 01 (Summon) uses a solid gold gradient button, while Cards 02–04 use thin outlined buttons, breaking the primary/secondary button grammar. The status sub-blocks are inconsistent: Card 02 has a 'BOUND 24/60' label, Card 03 has 'RIFT 07 ACTIVE' in red, and Card 04 has 'FORGE LV 6 82%'—these use different color treatments, alignment, and visual weight, so the cards read as four separate designs rather than one repeated unit. The large ghost numerals (01–04) collide with the card icons and the 'PRIMARY' pill, creating cluttered top-right corners. The 'CHOOSE YOUR PATH' heading is left-aligned to the card grid while '4 SANCTUMS' floats far to the right with no clear relationship, and the left hero column (title, tagline, 'THE DEEP TIDE' pill) has loose vertical rhythm with uneven gaps. The hero orb's diagonal light streak cuts across the layout and overlaps the card grid boundary, introducing a jarring, uncontrolled element. Typography mixes a serif display (Ætherwake, card titles) with a monospace UI face and a sans body, but the monospace is applied inconsistently (labels, numerals, footer) without a clear rule, and the gold 'shape the realm' inline emphasis in the body copy is a stray accent that doesn't match the system's semantic color roles.",
"suggestion":"1. Unify the card component: give all four cards identical internal structure (icon top-left, ghost numeral top-right, title, 2-line description, one status row, one action button) with consistent padding and a single shared border/radius/shadow token. 2. Establish a button system: make the primary action (Summon) the only filled gold button and all others a single consistent outlined style with identical height, corner radius, and label treatment. 3. Standardize the status row: one label style, one accent color per semantic state (e.g., gold for progress, red only for alert), aligned to the same baseline across all cards. 4. Reduce ghost-numeral prominence and reposition so it never overlaps the icon or pill; consider moving it to a fixed corner with reduced opacity. 5. Align 'CHOOSE YOUR PATH' and '4 SANCTUMS' into a single header row with a shared baseline and consistent left/right margins matching the card grid. 6. Tighten the left column vertical rhythm to a consistent 8px-based scale and constrain the hero orb's light streak so it stays within the hero region and does not bleed into the card grid. 7. Define a strict type scale: reserve the serif for display/titles, one sans for body, and monospace only for data/labels, and remove the stray gold inline emphasis in body copy in favor of a consistent semantic accent."
